Title: Defined normals from JSON were not used
Description: Hi,
I have a small JSON file with two colored triangles. Both triangles have different windings but the same normal vector. So I expect both with the same color / shading. But one triangle ist right colored, the other one is black.
It seems, that not the defined normals are used, but the normals are calculated by the winding of the vertices. What do I have to change to use the defined normals? Reason: I have a large set of triangles with switching windings. But I know the normals.

Btw: If I switch the first triangle definition from <code>80, 2, 1, 3, 0, 0,</code> to <code>80, 2, 3, 1, 0, 0,</code>, both windings are equal and the colors are perfect for both triangles. So I'm absolutely sure, that not the defined normals are used. How can I make three.js to use the normals from the JSON file?

